-*- coding:utf-8 -*-

vendor-probe-autocad-bricscad-divergences — real AutoCAD-vs-BricsCAD differences surfaced by the vendor probes
=============================================================================================================

Source: vendor:probes:autocad job 15538718100 (AutoCAD 2022, alfe 1.6.13,
Windows runner). With the no-&rest princ-capture fix (1.6.13) the AutoCAD probe
output is finally readable, and it now produces real verdicts. BricsCAD (macOS
+ Windows) is 100% green on the same probes; AutoCAD fails 14 assertions. These
are GENUINE BricsCAD-vs-AutoCAD divergences -- the whole point of the vendor
tail. clautolisp currently tracks BricsCAD's (more lenient) behaviour.

PROCESS (pjb) for EACH divergence below:
  1. Document it in autolisp-spec (per-vendor, in the *** vendor/clautolisp
     section of the affected function page + the user manual).
  2. Implement it per --dialect in clautolisp:
       --dialect autocad    -> AutoCAD's behaviour
       --dialect bricscad    -> BricsCAD's behaviour
       --dialect clautolisp -> a deliberate choice/extension (often the lenient
                               superset, possibly WARN)
       --dialect strict      -> the conservative/portable option (usually the
                               STRICTER of the two, so code that passes strict
                               runs on both vendors)
  3. Fork an issue to update cadaptor, which also tracks bricscad/autocad
     differences.
Each numbered divergence can be forked into its own spec+dialect+cadaptor issue.

DIAGNOSTIC GAP: the probes only print ok/FAIL, not the divergent VALUE. To spec
these accurately we need to SEE what AutoCAD actually returns (regapp -> nil or
T? entmakex on a marker-less ELLIPSE -> nil?). Add a diagnostic probe variant
(or a --verbose mode) that prints the actual return on a mismatch, and re-run on
AutoCAD, before finalising the spec wording.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Divergence 1 — entmake/entmakex requires subclass markers for R13+ entities
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Evidence (entity-lifecycle, 4 fails): entmakex returns nil (no ENAME) on AutoCAD
for ELLIPSE, LWPOLYLINE, RAY, XLINE; passes for LINE, POINT, CIRCLE, ARC, TEXT,
SOLID, 3DFACE. The probe's entmakex data for the failing four omits the
subclass-marker records, e.g.:
    (list (cons 0 "ELLIPSE") (cons 10 ...) (cons 11 ...) (cons 40 ..) ...)
i.e. no (100 . "AcDbEntity") / (100 . "AcDbEllipse").

Analysis: real AutoCAD's entmake/entmakex requires the group-100 subclass
markers for post-R12 entities (ELLIPSE, LWPOLYLINE, RAY, XLINE, MTEXT, LEADER,
SPLINE, HATCH, …); the R12-era entities (LINE/POINT/CIRCLE/ARC/TEXT/SOLID/
3DFACE/…) accept data without them. BricsCAD is lenient -- it synthesises the
markers -- and clautolisp follows BricsCAD.

Actions:
  * spec: document entmake's subclass-marker requirement; table of which entity
    types need (100 . "AcDbEntity")+(100 . "AcDb<Type>"). Note AutoCAD=required,
    BricsCAD=optional.
  * dialect: autocad -> reject (return nil) marker-less R13+ data; bricscad ->
    accept, synthesise markers; clautolisp -> accept (lenient), consider WARN;
    strict -> require markers (the portable choice, matches AutoCAD).
  * cadaptor fork.
Confidence: HIGH (well-documented AutoLISP behaviour).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Divergence 2 — regapp / XData round-trip (cascades to ssget "X" selection)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Evidence:
  * drawing-data: "regapp of a fresh app returns the name" FAILS
    -- the probe checks (= (regapp app) app).
  * selection: ALL EIGHT (mine)-XData-filtered ssget "X" tests fail
    (-3 app, type=LINE, type=LINE,CIRCLE, OR/AND/NOT colour, colour>1, and
    sslength=3). BUT "ssget X (-3 OTHERAPP) selects none" PASSES.
    (mine) = (-3 (app...)) XData filter over the seeded entities.

Analysis: ssget "X" itself works on AutoCAD (the OTHERAPP=0 case passed). The
seeded entities carry private XData under *app*, and the (mine) filter finds
NONE of them -> the regapp+XData-attach path diverges: either regapp returns a
different value (name vs nil vs T) and/or the XData set via entmod doesn't stick
/ isn't visible to the ssget -3 filter on AutoCAD as it is on BricsCAD.

Needs vendor confirmation of the exact difference (see DIAGNOSTIC GAP): print
(regapp app), and after seeding print (entget e '("*")) to see whether the -3
XData is actually attached on AutoCAD.

Actions: spec + dialect + cadaptor (same structure) once the exact behaviour is
captured. Likely two sub-divergences: (2a) regapp return value; (2b) XData
attach/visibility under ssget -3.
Confidence: MEDIUM (cascade root identified; exact vendor behaviour to confirm).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Divergence 3 — entmod on an XRECORD readback
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Evidence (drawing-data, 1 fail): "entmod on the xrecord reads back the new
value" fails. The probe entmakex's an XRECORD (with the (100 . "AcDbXrecord")
marker, so creation succeeds), then entmod-mutates it and reads it back; the
readback diverges on AutoCAD.

Analysis: entmod on a non-graphical dictionary object (XRECORD) may be
restricted or behave differently on AutoCAD vs BricsCAD (AutoCAD may require
the change via the dictionary / a different code path, or reject entmod on
xrecords). Confirm the actual readback.

Actions: spec + dialect + cadaptor. Confidence: MEDIUM.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Related
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The scenario dir already carries per-vendor expected captures
(entity-lifecycle-{autocad,bricscad}.sexp, etc.). Once each divergence's true
AutoCAD behaviour is confirmed, update the AutoCAD .sexp expectations to match,
so the conformance harness encodes the vendor difference rather than reporting
a raw FAIL. The vendor probes' single "ALL … PASSED" gate is fine for BricsCAD
(green) but for AutoCAD should become per-vendor-aware (expect the documented
divergences) OR the divergences get fixed in clautolisp's autocad dialect and
the probe data made portable (add the markers).

MEASURED values (job 15538912809, probes with failure-DIAG)
-----------------------------------------------------------
Diagnostics landed; the re-run gives the exact AutoCAD returns:

  D1 entmakex ELLIPSE/LWPOLYLINE/RAY/XLINE  -> type=nil val=nil  (rejected, not
     an error) -- CONFIRMED. AutoCAD requires (100 . "AcDb...") markers.
  D2 (regapp "CLAUTOLISP_DDP")              -> nil  (BricsCAD: the name).
     CONFIRMED. Registration still WORKS (selection DIAG shows the XData
     attaches), only the RETURN VALUE differs -- AutoCAD returns nil.
  D3 entmod on an XRECORD                   -> readback group1 = "payload"
     (the OLD value), want "payload2". CONFIRMED & sharper than thought:
     entmod on an xrecord is a NO-OP on AutoCAD (the mutation doesn't take);
     BricsCAD updates it. (Real AutoCAD wants xrecord edits via the object /
     vlax-put, not entmod.)
  Selection -> NOT a language divergence: DIAG shows the -3 XData attaches
     (YES) and ssget "X" filters, but mine-filter=8 (want 4) and ssget X
     all=36. Each probe opens a FRESH temp copy of empty.dwg, so the runner's
     c:/gitlab-runner/dwg/empty.dwg is CONTAMINATED -- ~32 stray entities, 4 of
     them already carrying the probe's private app XData (an ancient probe
     ._QSAVE, from before the temp-copy hygiene). => drawing-hygiene, not a
     divergence. BricsCAD passes (=4) because its empty.dwg copy is clean AND it
     uses _QUIT _N (no save).

Confirmed divergences to process (spec + dialect + cadaptor each):
  D1 entmake subclass markers for R13+ entities   (autocad reject / bricscad
     synthesise / clautolisp lenient+WARN / strict require).   *** DONE ***
  D2 regapp  -- NOT a divergence: CONTAMINATION. See below.
  D3 entmod on non-graphical XRECORD: autocad no-op, bricscad updates.  *** DONE ***

D1 IMPLEMENTED (clautolisp 1.6.16). entity-family gains a since-r13-p flag;
clautolisp.drawing:entity-dxf-missing-markers (pure) reports the absent
(100 . "AcDb...") markers; the mock host applies a per-dialect policy in
%host-add-entity (autocad-2026/strict reject -> nil+ERRNO 36; clautolisp warn
[entmake-subclass-marker]; bricscad-v26/lax accept+synthesise). Spec: R13+
marker note in the ENTMAKE + ENTMAKEX *** clautolisp sections. Tests: drawing
unit + builtins-core per-dialect e2e (all green). STILL TODO for D1: fork the
cadaptor issue.

D3 IMPLEMENTED (clautolisp 1.6.17; renamed mock-host -> cador in 1.7.27).
Mirrors D1 exactly, sharing the same per-dialect resolver. The cador host
gates host-entmod (clautolisp/cador/source/entity-api.lisp): the pure
predicate %entmod-target-nongraphical-p flags a non-graphical target (the
drawing layer's XRECORD/DICTIONARY families carry :graphical-p nil), and
%resolved-divergence-policy (shared with D1) maps the ambient dialect
(clautolisp.autolisp-runtime:current-evaluation-dialect-name) to an action:
autocad-2026 / clautolisp / strict -> :normative NO-OP (entmod returns nil,
the mutation does not take, matching AutoCAD); bricscad-v26 / lax -> :deviant
apply (matching BricsCAD). strict + bricscad-v26 additionally emit the
[entmod-nongraphical] warning; lax is silent. Spec: ENTMOD page ****
"Non-graphical objects (resolved divergence — chapter 25 case 2)" in the
autolisp-visual-lisp-specification-draft. Tests (all green, verified
2026-08-06, builtins-core suite 1712 checks 0 fail): builtins-core e2e
dd-d3-normative-dialects-noop-entmod-on-xrecord /
dd-d3-deviant-dialects-apply-entmod-on-xrecord /
dd-d3-warns-under-bricscad-and-strict-only /
dd-d3-graphical-entmod-unaffected-by-object-gate, plus the cador host unit
dictsearch-object-feeds-entmod-and-entget. STILL TODO for D3: fork the
cadaptor issue (same external follow-on as D1).

D2 RESOLVED as contamination, NOT a divergence. regapp of an ALREADY-registered
app returns nil on BOTH AutoCAD and BricsCAD (that is the spec) -- the probe's
fixed app name "CLAUTOLISP_DDP" was already in the drawing's APPID table from a
prior run (there is no unregapp; clean-slate only deletes entities), so the
"fresh" assumption was false. Proven when BricsCAD Windows ALSO failed the same
regapp assertion (job 15539173366). Fixed by a per-run-unique app name in the
probe (commit "probes: unique regapp app name"). No spec/dialect change.

Actions before Divergence 2/3 spec text is final: none -- the values are now
measured. Selection: regenerate a truly-empty c:/gitlab-runner/dwg/empty.dwg on
the runner (and consider making the AutoCAD probe save-free like BricsCAD:
run.scr `._QSAVE`/`._QUIT _Y` -> `._QUIT _N`, tested carefully for the
accoreconsole prompt) then re-run to confirm selection is green / surfaces any
real ssget "X" divergence underneath.

